<figure class="ga-chain not-prose" aria-label="Three-stage attack chain with self-sustaining feedback loop">
  <p class="ga-chain-eyebrow">Attack chain</p>

  <div class="ga-chain-stages">
    <div class="ga-chain-stage">
      <span class="num">01</span>
      <strong>Credential harvest</strong>
      <p>AiTM proxy at <code>my-github[.]com</code> captures real GitHub login, MFA included. Victim authenticates against the real backend through the proxy.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ga-chain-stage is-hot">
      <span class="num">02</span>
      <strong>OAuth token theft</strong>
      <p>Injected script triggers device flow (<code>Ov23ctrqCqZ79UaYKwyq</code>), auto-fills code, auto-approves consent.<br/>Scopes: <code>repo</code> <code>workflow</code> <code>read:org</code></p>
    </div>

    <div class="ga-chain-stage">
      <span class="num">03</span>
      <strong>Token exfiltration</strong>
      <p>Token + username sent to <code>my-github[.]com:8443/t</code> via <code>no-cors</code> GET (fire-and-forget). Token survives password resets and session revocations.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ga-chain-down" aria-hidden="true">
    <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5v14"/><path d="m19 12-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
  </div>

  <div class="ga-chain-loop">
    <span class="ga-chain-loop-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M1 4v6h6"/><path d="M3.51 15a9 9 0 1 0 2.13-9.36L1 10"/></svg>
    </span>
    <p class="ga-chain-loop-text">
      The granted scopes are enough to push workflows like <strong>security-audit.yml</strong>, which send CI/CD secrets to the same server. I did not observe a phished token being used this way.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figcaption>The only way to kill these tokens is to revoke the OAuth app itself.</figcaption>
</figure>
